field contradicts the lockfile: Pnpm (packageManager in package.json) version=10.4.1
    note: packageManager in package.json says pnpm, but yarn.lock belongs to another package manager; using pnpm
field resolves lockfiles of two managers: Pnpm (packageManager in package.json) version=10.4.1
unsupported packageManager: Pnpm (lockfile pnpm-lock.yaml)
    note: packageManager "deno@2.5.0" in package.json is not npm, pnpm, yarn or bun; ignored
    note: no packageManager field; detected pnpm from pnpm-lock.yaml. Add "packageManager": "pnpm@<version>" to package.json
yarn 4, Plug'n'Play without .pnp.cjs: YarnBerry (packageManager in package.json) version=4.5.0 linker=Pnp
    note: yarn Plug'n'Play is enabled but .pnp.cjs is missing; run `yarn install`
yarn 4, Plug'n'Play installed: YarnBerry (packageManager in package.json) version=4.5.0 linker=Pnp
yarn 4, node-modules linker: YarnBerry (packageManager in package.json) version=4.5.0 linker=NodeModules
yarn 1 by version over a 2+ lockfile header: YarnClassic (packageManager in package.json) version=1.22.22
field above the workspace root is not used: Npm (default)
    note: no packageManager field or lockfile; using npm. Add "packageManager": "<manager>@<version>" to packages/package.json
